{
  "_doc": [
    "Route-render audit manifest (SYSTEM_MAP.md \u00a713.5 enforcement layer).",
    "scripts/audit_route_render.py loads every route in `routes` on LIVE",
    "production post-deploy and asserts the rendered DOM: the title must",
    "contain `title_contains`, must NOT be the marketing-homepage title",
    "(unless allow_homepage_title \u2014 that catches the _redirects/Functions",
    "fallthrough class that hid the launch interstitial for 13 days), and",
    "`selector` (when set) must appear in the DOM within 15s.",
    "",
    "DISCOVERY CONTRACT: the script also walks the repo for static SPA",
    "routes (portal/*, admin/*, education/*, root pages). Every discovered",
    "route MUST appear either in `routes` (with real assertions) or in",
    "`unaudited` (a conscious, diff-visible exemption). A new page route",
    "that ships without touching this file FAILS THE DEPLOY \u2014 that is the",
    "point: \u00a70.2.1 visual verification is a machine gate, not discipline.",
    "Parameterized Function-served routes (launch, NPS, admin cases) are",
    "audited via tokenized paths below; their static dirs sit in unaudited."
  ],
